Block IP-literal hosts and redirects to non-public addresses

The SSRF guard in lib/fetch.js filters addresses inside the DNS `lookup`, and
Node never calls `lookup` for a host that is already an IP. A URL such as
`http://127.1/`, `http://0x7f000001/` or `http://user@[::1]/`, or a public page
that redirects to one, reaches internal addresses. `IGNORE_DOMAINS_RE` misses
the same URLs, because its regexps are anchored right after `https?://` and the
userinfo shifts the host.

Upstream itteco/iframely 8ab98c12 (#738), after v26.11.13. A `beforeRequest`
hook in the patched @adobe/fetch checks every request and every followed
redirect; ignore regexps also run against the URL with userinfo stripped.
`ALLOWED_LOCAL_HOSTS` exempts named hosts.

Drop on the bump to the first upstream tag that contains 8ab98c12: quilt then
reports it as already applied.

Covered by `test/ssrf.js`.
